    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n58 St. Brendan's Park is a beautifully extended and recently renovated three-bedroom, two-bathroom semi-detached family home presented in turnkey condition. This exceptional property has been thoughtfully upgraded through an architect-led renovation, creating a stylish and highly functional home ideally suited to modern family living. Extending to approximately 137 sq. m. (1,475 sq. ft.), the house combines generous proportions, quality finishes and an excellent location just off the Malahide Road. With further potential to extend (subject to planning permission), this is a home that will appeal to a wide range of discerning buyers.\n\nAccommodation \n\nThe accommodation is both well-balanced and versatile. On entering, the entrance hall provides a welcoming introduction to the home. To the right of the hall is the converted garage, currently used as a home office, but equally suitable as a fourth bedroom, playroom or home gym. To the left of the hall lies a cosy reception room, featuring a wood-burning stove, creating a warm and inviting retreat. To the rear, the home opens into an impressive open-plan kitchen, living and dining space, flooded with natural light and enjoying beautiful views over the garden. This space is ideal for family life and entertaining, featuring Trunk flooring throughout. The bespoke solid wood in-frame kitchen is finished with quartz worktops, Carrara marble tiled floors and splashback, and includes a range cooker and central island. A cloakroom and WC with a utility area complete the ground floor accommodation.\n\nUpstairs, there are three bedrooms comprising two generous doubles and a single bedroom, all benefiting from built-in wardrobes. A recently installed family bathroom with a marble sink and high-quality finishes serves this level. A new combi-boiler ensures constant hot water and excellent water pressure throughout the home.\n\nGardens \n\nTo the front, there is off-street parking for two cars. A side entrance provides access to the expansive, split-level rear garden, which is sure to impress buyers with its beautiful garden views and sense of space. The garden enjoys excellent sunlight throughout the day, featuring a sun-trapped terrace ideal for morning coffee and a further seating area to the end of the garden, perfectly positioned to enjoy the evening sun. An EV charger is installed to the side of the garden, adding to the home's modern convenience.\n\nLocation\n\nSt Brendan's Park is a mature and highly sought-after residential location in Artane, just off the Malahide Road. The area is extremely well serviced by public transport, with excellent bus routes on the doorstep including the 15, 27, 42, 43 and N6. Both Killester and Harmonstown DART stations are within walking distance, while the M1 and M50 are easily accessible, and Dublin Airport is approximately 20 minutes away.\n\nThe property is also within a short walk of the wonderful St Anne's Park and is surrounded by a wide selection of well-regarded primary and secondary schools, making it an ideal choice for families. A range of local shops, cafés and amenities are also close by, further enhancing the appeal of this superb home.\n\nIf you would like a viewing, please email us or call the office on 01 8336555 to arrange an appointment. If you wish to place an offer, please visit www.sherryfitz.ie where you can register to make an offer on this property."
      },
